+# A pressed on Cancel, in the two panels that answer A themselves.
+#
+# CSWGuiInGameSoloModeQuery and CSWGuiOptionsResolution implement the raw A,
+# 0x27, at panel level and never read which button has focus, so A on Cancel
+# confirmed: Solo Mode turned on, the highlighted resolution was applied. Issue
+# #21. Each hook sits on the panel's HandleInputEvent (vtable+0x3C) at its
+# entry, where the event and its value are still the two stack arguments, and
+# when A arrives with Cancel focused it rewrites the event to 0x28 -- B. The
+# panel's own dispatcher then takes its own Cancel path, and A on OK reaches the
+# vanilla confirm untouched.
+#
+# NOT a consumed exit, which is what these hooks were until 2026-09-24 and why
+# Solo Mode then refused on both buttons. KPM's wrapper runs the stolen bytes
+# BEFORE its `TEST EAX,EAX` (Kotor-Patch-Manager, wrapper_x86.cpp, "EXECUTE
+# STOLEN ORIGINAL BYTES"). The Solo hook sat on `mov eax,[0x7A39FC]`, so the test
+# read the app pointer, never the handler's answer, and every A took the close
+# path. The resolution hook's stolen `push 0` reached its exit with an extra
+# dword on an ESP-relative frame. tools/check_hook_stolen_bytes.py now refuses
+# both shapes.
