+# LEA for a stack source), which is what lets the handler rewrite the event.
+# ECX is the panel: these are __thiscall entries. Stolen bytes run after the
+# handler with every register restored, so the rewritten slot is what the
+# dispatcher's own `mov eax,[esp+4]` / `mov eax,[ebp+8]` then reads.
